WEBVTT

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:19.920
Sir Yokomichi!

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:21.580
Don't call me by my old name!

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.550
Go, ninja boy! Go and steal Ms. Scarred away!

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:27.760
You got it!

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:43.020
<i>Wait for me, Master Mary!</i>

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:26.080
I-I'm going to go all out!

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:31.710
Pinch mode!

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:37.140
Is that your t-true art style?!

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:40.220
I can't lose!

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:45.350
How sublime!

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:48.060
I love women who can't lose.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:51.820
And since I can't lose, I'm the most sublime!

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:53.280
What gives?

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:58.120
You see, no matter how harsh the environment may be,

00:02:58.120 --> 00:02:59.740
it cannot crush a flower.

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:03.330
Even if snow or sand try to bury it, with the coming of spring,

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:05.290
the flower will climb toward the sun and blossom.

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:11.170
That is why when such flowers bloom, people describe them as blooming with pride.

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:18.390
You're a pretty good gal, so I'll let you in on something.

00:03:18.390 --> 00:03:20.510
There's dance inside of you!

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:22.850
It's inside everyone!

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:24.770
Fire more!

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:28.150
Why am I in such a pinch?!

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:30.610
Are we neck-and-neck just before the deadline?!

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.440
It's like getting orders before I've submitted the manuscript!

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:43.290
This will finish you off!

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:45.120
I wouldn't be so sure.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:49.540
What's that?!

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:50.710
Herrlich!

00:03:52.550 --> 00:03:54.510
Submit for publishing!

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:03.310
H-Here I go!

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:04.270
Cecil?!

00:04:04.270 --> 00:04:07.190
Dudley, that was a close call...

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:12.150
Even I couldn't possibly catch her!

00:04:13.110 --> 00:04:16.150
Show backbone!

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:22.160
W-W-We have accomplished what needed to be done.

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:25.410
Due to outside intervention, I'd say this was a no-contest.

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:27.830
Are you sure that's okay?

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:31.420
Her Majesty will deal with the remaining battle.

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:36.010
Master Scarred!

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:40.720
Afraid not.

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:43.140
Please leave!

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:47.060
I will keep her busy, so please leave!

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:52.810
Enough with the lies, Master Mary.

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:57.240
What are you saying?! I am Mary!

00:04:57.240 --> 00:04:59.280
Silence, you phony!

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:02.780
Master Mary has a slightly larger bosom!

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:03.870
Big...

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:04.530
Busted...

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:05.490
Blond!

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:08.660
That is what people call the ultimate truth.

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:14.210
You cannot hide the ultimate truth with that crappy disguise!

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:15.920
Why don't we stop watching?

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:17.090
Okay? Okay?

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:22.470
So we had a distinguishing feature aside from those scars!

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:24.850
Mary, you won the bet.

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:26.430
You get five minutes.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:28.850
Enjoy your last scene on stage!

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:32.730
M-Master Mary!

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:34.190
Y-Yes!

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:37.190
For me, I find you are wantly!

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:40.400
Wantly?

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:44.120
I-I meant to say you are as beautiful as a water lily!

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:52.420
If I was a color, would you say I'm red or white?

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:53.580
Wh-White!

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:57.090
You mustn't say that!

00:05:57.090 --> 00:06:00.880
Many lives have been lost thus far, all for this execution!

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:04.260
Many have died and many have fallen due to my own hands.

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:07.180
So it is my responsibility to become a sacrifice!

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:08.310
It is not!

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:13.440
Citizens of the Far East want to save those embraced by an unfair fate to die.

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:14.560
We do not merely gaze out to the future,

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:20.190
content to spout pretty nonsense like claiming that their deaths will lead to salvation!

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:21.320
You're naïve!

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:23.740
This is the current way of the world.

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:29.540
Through historical reenactments, we have changed war and even history into cards for negotiation.

00:06:29.540 --> 00:06:34.960
Then we will conquer the world and change the way things work!

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:38.340
But I'm covered in all these scars.

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:39.250
I don't care!

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:43.260
Historical reenactments have made me marry and divorce several times!

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:44.550
I'm vulgar!

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:45.340
I don't care!

00:06:45.640 --> 00:06:48.350
It may turn all of England against you!

00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:49.510
I don't care!

00:06:50.060 --> 00:06:53.060
Some of us have already turned the entire world against us.

00:06:53.060 --> 00:06:58.110
No matter who dies for you, it does <i>not</i> make you obligated to die in return!

00:06:58.110 --> 00:06:59.110
But...

00:06:59.110 --> 00:06:59.770
Enough!

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:04.950
Even if this isn't what you want and you try to resist, I swear I shall steal you away!

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:10.950
But why...?

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:13.960
Why didn't you kiss me back there?!

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:14.790
Wha—

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:20.460
You didn't kiss me earlier, so I felt certain you had dumped me...

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:23.260
And now you have the nerve to say all of this?!

00:07:23.260 --> 00:07:27.180
Tenzo, explain why you didn't kiss her, even if it's just a lie!

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:28.390
J-Judge!

00:07:29.390 --> 00:07:30.600
Master Mary...

00:07:30.890 --> 00:07:34.930
In the Far East, locking lips seals a couple's marriage engagement.

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:37.600
So it is not something to be taken lightly.

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:41.940
B-But doesn't that mean you didn't want to marry me?!

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:46.990
At that time, I was still unsure of whether you were a good match for me or not.

00:07:46.990 --> 00:07:48.700
A good match?

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:50.320
Is there a test or something?

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:53.290
Judge. It is simple.

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:55.290
First, take a deep breath!

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:06.970
You <i>pass</i>!

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:12.430
Master Mary, I have fallen heels over head for you!

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:17.940
Judge!

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:19.600
Me too!

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:34.490
Come here.

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:36.250
Master Tenzo!

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:44.750
I lost, didn't I?

00:08:46.590 --> 00:08:48.760
I have lost as well.

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:07.190
Master Tenzo, would you be kind enough to scar me?

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:12.320
Judge, if you would hold pride in those scars.

00:09:21.170 --> 00:09:24.380
Mary, the show is over.

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:29.050
The Fairy Queen's Wings of Light?!

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:34.760
What a display of power!

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:37.010
How do you think Tenzo is going to pull out of this one?

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:38.560
He should have a plan.

00:09:39.230 --> 00:09:41.890
<i>Put everything on it, Crossunite!</i>

00:09:43.480 --> 00:09:48.190
Fairies that descend to where humans dwell can no longer return to the forest.

00:09:48.190 --> 00:09:53.110
Just as the mermaid turned to foam and vanished, I will pluck all the water lilies here!

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:54.740
That line!

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:57.990
I dare you to say it again after Master Mary pulls out that sword!

00:09:57.990 --> 00:10:01.250
B-But I couldn't pull that sword out.

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:05.630
What are you plotting?!

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:08.960
I have a request for the sword that protects England!

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:12.880
O' Excalibur, entrusted with the fair folk, yet nonetheless broken!

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:17.350
Emerge from the fair folk's dimension and leave your Earth Pulse sheath!

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:24.730
It came out?

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:26.770
What are those?!

00:10:27.150 --> 00:10:31.740
They are the Excalibur Collbrande.

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:35.780
If the Spirit Realm bequeathed two Excaliburs unto us,

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:39.950
then Collbrande needed to be mended in the Spirit Realm.

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:44.000
In other words, it was in the Earth Pulse,

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:48.380
inside the light emitted by Excalibur Caliburn!

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:52.630
Then are you implying that Caliburn was the key to Collbrande's storage?!

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:56.760
"We will consider he who realize that worthy to be our king."

00:10:56.760 --> 00:10:58.050
You are exactly right.

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:02.810
Well, you have both pulled out one of the twin Excalibur swords!

00:11:03.310 --> 00:11:06.230
How will England respond to having two women fit to be king?!

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:10.770
Fairy Queen, I would like to propose a truce!

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:13.490
Fairy Queen, you may keep your crown.

00:11:13.490 --> 00:11:16.110
We hope that you will allow Mary to seek asylum in Musashi.

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:16.780
What?!

00:11:17.450 --> 00:11:19.660
I want you to recall what the Testament says.

00:11:19.660 --> 00:11:23.450
Soon after this, you will designate your nephew to be your heir.

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:29.250
In other words, you just need to designate Mary and Crossunite's child as the next king of England!

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:35.590
The Far East would support England if it defends itself through birthing new life rather than bringing death.

00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:39.050
Crossunite, bring Mary back with you safe and sound!

00:11:39.390 --> 00:11:42.430
And Mary, are you willing to transfer here?

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:43.520
Judge!

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:45.310
Why?!

00:11:45.310 --> 00:11:47.190
You'll understand once you die.

00:11:47.480 --> 00:11:50.190
Thanks to you, I was able to make it this far.

00:11:50.190 --> 00:11:52.730
Next time, it will be my turn to kill you.

00:11:52.730 --> 00:11:55.900
I will do so by giving birth to a child who will steal your throne.

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:59.200
And after that, let's play together again!

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:01.120
Let's play in our Avalon.

00:12:01.870 --> 00:12:05.330
This is London, England, the Fairy Queen's city.

00:12:05.790 --> 00:12:09.880
Fairies who wished to become human cannot stay here.

00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:14.260
I will protect your dreams while in a city of humans!

00:12:14.840 --> 00:12:17.720
Elizabeth, you are my other half...

00:12:17.720 --> 00:12:19.050
My precious little sister.

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:29.270
Sister!

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:32.980
Thank you!

00:12:42.370 --> 00:12:43.580
Please don't look at me!

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:47.330
There is nothing wrong with looking at you.

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:01.760
So history will remain unchanged?

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:06.390
This is where we will conclude the Spanish Armada battle.

00:13:15.190 --> 00:13:15.940
Isn't that...?

00:13:18.280 --> 00:13:20.030
It's the admiral's ship!

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:32.500
<i>Twenty-five years ago, I...</i>

00:13:33.790 --> 00:13:35.500
<i>I failed to protect everyone then, too.</i>

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:37.090
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:13:37.090 --> 00:13:41.340
<i>And here I had promised to take you to Falles once I returned from Lepanto.</i>

00:13:42.260 --> 00:13:44.970
<i>You won't have to suffer any longer, </i>

00:13:45.680 --> 00:13:46.810
Juana...

00:13:46.810 --> 00:13:48.680
You called, Chancellor?

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:49.850
Juana?!

00:13:49.850 --> 00:13:52.940
Tes. I came on the San Martin to retrieve you.

00:13:54.610 --> 00:13:58.440
If I go back, Tres España will be made to suffer!

00:13:59.030 --> 00:14:00.490
So I should pass away and—

00:14:00.490 --> 00:14:01.610
Why?!

00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:03.320
Juana?

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:04.820
What would it take

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:07.620
to make you cherish the present more than the past?

00:14:08.790 --> 00:14:12.960
I-I just want to help the person who saved me.

00:14:12.960 --> 00:14:15.210
I'm always thinking about how I want to be with you!

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:19.170
So why must I revert to my old self

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:21.220
when I want to speak with you?!

00:14:21.970 --> 00:14:23.680
And now you're abandoning me?

00:14:24.130 --> 00:14:25.930
Nothing could be more frustrating!

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:34.270
Are you all right?

00:14:34.270 --> 00:14:35.600
I'm sorry.

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:38.110
This is about all I'm good for.

00:14:38.110 --> 00:14:40.280
That alone is enough!

00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:42.110
Please continue to do so forever!

00:14:42.570 --> 00:14:43.110
Wait—

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:47.030
Vice-President, hurry and take the Chancellor to—

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:51.200
It's not—

00:14:51.540 --> 00:14:53.330
Let's just leave it at that.

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:55.040
Wh-Whoa, you jump to conclusions fast!

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:58.040
Now, Juana! That wasn't fair.

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:03.510
Let's go.

00:15:03.510 --> 00:15:06.260
The Spanish Armada battle isn't over yet.

00:15:11.060 --> 00:15:13.770
Our main objective for the freshly resumed Spanish Armada battle

00:15:14.390 --> 00:15:18.520
is to force Tres Espana to retreat and obtain victory.

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:22.110
In that vein, we'll need to suppress their Aerial God of War Corps,

00:15:22.110 --> 00:15:24.530
force the enemy's main fleet to cease cannon fire,

00:15:24.530 --> 00:15:27.110
and intercept the enemy's amphibious troops.

00:15:27.660 --> 00:15:32.080
Our main obstacle will be to sink the enemy flagship, the San Martin.

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:35.250
Do we have to fight that stealth warship?

00:15:36.870 --> 00:15:41.130
Remember how that warship damaged Musashi before we reached England?

00:15:41.130 --> 00:15:43.300
If we don't pulverize them here and now,

00:15:43.300 --> 00:15:46.630
it'll be a thorn in our side when we try to hold negotiations with other nations later.

00:15:49.470 --> 00:15:50.550
Listen everyone.

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:53.430
The second Spanish Armada battle is about to begin!

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:18.620
The guy with parted hair and glasses gave it to us?

00:16:21.420 --> 00:16:25.050
Oh, but didn't Shiro check over everything?

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:28.220
In that case, I'm confident they must be something nice!

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:40.350
Okay, everyone! I'm counting on you!

00:16:58.960 --> 00:17:01.170
They can't hit me if I'm up— What?!

00:17:18.020 --> 00:17:20.350
I may not have Malga's guidance, but...

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:21.980
Herrlich!

00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:33.780
Low-speed bullet incoming from the northwest at 10:00 above the portside!

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:37.200
The attack is coming from the stealth warship, San Martin. Over.

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:38.330
Here it comes.

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:40.080
Expand defense.

00:17:40.080 --> 00:17:42.330
We will knock it away. Over.

00:17:47.300 --> 00:17:48.300
Our shot passed through them!

00:17:48.590 --> 00:17:52.220
San Martin has left the relevant area. Over.

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:55.680
What made that first sound of fire?

00:17:55.680 --> 00:17:57.180
Please rest at ease.

00:17:57.180 --> 00:17:59.100
We successfully deflected that attack. Over.

00:18:01.520 --> 00:18:06.770
Lady Adele, San Martin is most likely moving toward portside stern. Over.

00:18:06.770 --> 00:18:08.940
Position the cannons to face 7:00!

00:18:14.410 --> 00:18:15.320
Cannon fire.

00:18:15.660 --> 00:18:16.160
Canno—

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:17.200
Low-speed bullet incoming! Canno—

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:19.330
It's headed toward our starboard side. Over.

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:27.920
Small vessels have been identified!

00:18:27.920 --> 00:18:29.630
They are docking on us. Over.

00:18:47.310 --> 00:18:52.110
If we take out their bridge, this ship will stop and Musashi won't be able to move anymore.

00:18:52.490 --> 00:18:54.530
Men, follow after me!

00:18:54.530 --> 00:18:55.240
Tes!

00:18:57.620 --> 00:18:59.580
We will deflect it. Over.

00:19:03.710 --> 00:19:06.080
That shot was fired by the amphibious troops to cover for them.

00:19:06.710 --> 00:19:11.550
I suspect the San Martin has already moved to Takao's stern.

00:19:12.170 --> 00:19:17.180
However, something feels different with the relationship between the San Martin's first and second shots

00:19:17.180 --> 00:19:22.810
and the relationship between their second and third shots. Over.

00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:26.400
Fire!

00:19:27.560 --> 00:19:28.770
Incoming low-speed bullet!

00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:31.570
Headed toward the port bow, straight toward Asakusa. Over.

00:19:33.820 --> 00:19:35.030
The opposite side?!

00:19:35.030 --> 00:19:38.410
Musashino, how fast can the San Martin move?

00:19:38.410 --> 00:19:42.200
At full speed, it should be able to cover that distance.

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:46.620
However, it is impossible for them to move at full speed without notice.

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:49.330
Could it be?

00:19:57.680 --> 00:20:02.010
They're using a barrage of cannon fire to force the San Martin to move toward their port!

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:06.770
But that just means you have to take the bridge before they succeed, right?

00:20:06.770 --> 00:20:09.060
Yeah, the game is on!

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:10.520
Indeed, the game is on!

00:20:10.520 --> 00:20:12.400
This is the time to spend money.

00:20:14.780 --> 00:20:17.610
You should give my bats a try while you're at it.

00:20:18.360 --> 00:20:19.950
They land good hits.

00:20:20.700 --> 00:20:27.160
With this barrage, our Inadequate HQ will most assuredly sink your stealth warship.

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:28.120
That's quite the loss.

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:32.590
It doesn't really matter if you find the San Martin.

00:20:32.590 --> 00:20:35.920
We jumped aboard with the intent to take your ship.

00:20:35.920 --> 00:20:38.760
So play with us a bit, merchant.

00:20:40.640 --> 00:20:43.600
Takao is being fired at from the starboard side. Over.

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:46.850
Both sides, take aim!

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:51.730
Fire!

00:20:52.650 --> 00:20:54.520
I will commence barrier purification!

00:21:00.410 --> 00:21:01.450
Goodness.

00:21:01.450 --> 00:21:02.820
There were two ships?

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:05.990
When it looks like we're about to locate the San Martin,

00:21:05.990 --> 00:21:10.040
the other San Martin fires from the opposite side and throws us into confusion.

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:13.250
Come on! Let's trash the San Martins in one go!

00:21:19.590 --> 00:21:22.550
The same one is coming! It's the first one!

00:21:22.550 --> 00:21:26.350
But the first ship just pulled around behind us...

00:21:26.350 --> 00:21:30.480
Lady Suzu, what do you mean by the first one? Over.

00:21:30.480 --> 00:21:33.940
Huh? By first, I mean it's the first one.

00:21:34.310 --> 00:21:37.150
From before we came to England.

00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:39.440
It can't be! It's still here?!

00:21:42.950 --> 00:21:44.240
Defenses to the bow!

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:50.370
Isn't that Grace O'Malley?!

00:21:51.870 --> 00:21:53.830
I'm returning the favor, Musashi!

00:21:58.510 --> 00:22:00.720
I appreciate it, Grace!

00:22:01.050 --> 00:22:02.840
Proceed with battle!

00:22:09.810 --> 00:22:10.770
Pedro! Look out!

00:22:10.770 --> 00:22:11.810
What is it—

00:22:15.230 --> 00:22:17.110
You forgot that, so I gave it back.

00:22:17.110 --> 00:22:20.570
I'll punch you three times and defeat the Valdés Siblings!

00:22:23.740 --> 00:22:25.240
How can I help you?

00:22:25.620 --> 00:22:28.620
Restitution for my husband, Lord Tachibana Muneshige.

00:22:29.950 --> 00:22:34.330
Oh! Lord Tachibana was kind enough to teach me much, as I was quite green.

00:22:35.080 --> 00:22:37.210
If I were to use an English term to cover my embarrassment,

00:22:38.250 --> 00:22:40.260
I'd say we had sex together.
